#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.after"
msgid "A decision you, or the world, settled says what happened to it rather than leaving."
msgstr "Kad je nešto odlučeno, bilo od tebe ili od sveta, obaveštenje kaže šta se desilo, umesto da samo nestane."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.answer"
msgid "Alerts tell you what happened and what needs you; the game always shows them, and this device can too."
msgstr "Obaveštenja ti kažu šta se desilo i šta traži tebe; igra ih uvek prikazuje, a može i ovaj uređaj."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.line"
msgid "What you are told, and where."
msgstr "Šta ti se javlja i gde."

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.step1.how"
msgid "open Alerts from Home: Waiting on you first, then Important, then the rest by day."
msgstr "otvori Obaveštenja sa Početne: prvo Čeka te, zatim Važno, pa ostalo po danima."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.step1.to"
msgid "To read them"
msgstr "Da ih pročitaš"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.step2.how"
msgid "press it: it opens the thing itself, and Back returns to the list."
msgstr "pritisni ga: otvara se sama stvar, a Nazad te vraća na spisak."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.step2.to"
msgid "To act on one"
msgstr "Da postupiš po jednom"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.step3.how"
msgid "open Settings, then Alerts, turn on alerts on this device, and choose which kinds reach it."
msgstr "otvori Podešavanja, pa Obaveštenja, uključi obaveštenja na ovom uređaju i izaberi koje vrste stižu na njega."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.step3.to"
msgid "To get them on this device"
msgstr "Da ih dobijaš na ovom uređaju"

#. Everyday words a player might type into Help's search to find this page, separated by commas. Give the words people in your language would search with, and add others if you like. Keep the commas.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.synonyms"
msgid "alert, notification, notify, push, phone, news"
msgstr "obaveštenje, obaveštenja, obavestenja, notifikacije, notifikacija, upozorenje, alert, push, telefon, vesti"

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.title"
msgid "How alerts work"
msgstr "Kako rade obaveštenja"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.word1.means"
msgid "News that changes your country or your things, such as a war."
msgstr "Vesti koje menjaju tvoju državu ili tvoje stvari, na primer rat."

#. A word this page explains, shown in bold above its meaning.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.alerts.word1.term"
msgid "Important"
msgstr "Važno"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.assemblyMember.line"
msgid "Votes on every bill, and may propose one."
msgstr "Glasa o svakom predlogu zakona i može da predloži neki."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.assemblyMember.p1"
msgid "<b>A member votes on every bill before the chamber, and may propose bills.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Član glasa o svakom predlogu zakona pred Skupštinom i može da predlaže zakone.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.assemblyMember.p2"
msgid "Seats are elected by place: a member stands for where their voters live, for the term the constitution sets."
msgstr "Mesta se biraju po oblastima: član zastupa oblast u kojoj žive njegovi birači, na mandat koji određuje ustav."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.assemblyMember.p3"
msgid "To vote: the seat’s console under You lists each bill waiting on your vote, with its tally and when it closes."
msgstr "Da glasaš: konzola tvog mesta pod Ti navodi svaki predlog zakona koji čeka tvoj glas, sa trenutnim stanjem glasova i rokom zatvaranja."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.assemblyMember.p4"
msgid "Your votes are public, and the console keeps them: every bill you voted on, and how it ended."
msgstr "Tvoji glasovi su javni, a konzola ih čuva: svaki predlog uz tvoj glas i kako je završio."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.assemblyMember.title"
msgid "What does a member of the Assembly do?"
msgstr "Šta radi član Skupštine?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.bankFounding.line"
msgid "What it takes, and what is spent."
msgstr "Šta je potrebno i šta se troši."

#. {level} is a player level. {charter} is the charter fee, drawn as a coin amount. {capital} is the least capital, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.bankFounding.p1"
msgid "From level {level} you can found a bank from You › Start something. It takes a {charter} charter fee, which is spent, and at least {capital} of your own money, which becomes the bank’s cash."
msgstr "Od nivoa {level} možeš da osnuješ banku u odeljku Ti › Pokreni nešto. Potrebna je taksa za osnivanje od {charter}, koja se troši, i najmanje {capital} tvog novca, koji postaje gotovina banke."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.bankFounding.p2"
msgid "A bank can fail, and the people who bank there can lose money. You can wind a bank up, but founding one cannot be undone."
msgstr "Banka može da propadne, a ljudi koji u njoj drže novac mogu da ga izgube. Banku možeš da zatvoriš, ali osnivanje ne može da se poništi."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.bankFounding.title"
msgid "How do I start a bank?"
msgstr "Kako da osnujem banku?"

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.bankRunning.li1"
msgid "<b>What it lends on:</b> published terms. Anyone who fits them borrows without asking you. You can change them, or take them down; loans already made stay as they are."
msgstr "<b>Pod kojim uslovima daje kredite:</b> objavljeni uslovi. Ko god ih ispunjava, uzima kredit a da te ne pita. Možeš da ih promeniš ili da ih skineš; već odobreni krediti ostaju kakvi jesu."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.bankRunning.li2"
msgid "<b>Offer someone a loan:</b> the money leaves the bank only when they accept. One offer at a time to one person; you can withdraw it while it waits."
msgstr "<b>Ponudi nekome kredit:</b> novac napušta banku tek kad osoba prihvati ponudu. Jedna ponuda odjednom jednoj osobi; možeš da je povučeš dok čeka."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.bankRunning.li3"
msgid "<b>Who owes it money:</b> each loan and how it is going. A loan nobody repays is a loss nothing makes good."
msgstr "<b>Ko joj duguje novac:</b> svaki kredit i kako se otplaćuje. Kredit koji niko ne vrati je gubitak koji ništa ne nadoknađuje."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.bankRunning.line"
msgid "Whether it can pay out, who owes it, and its terms."
msgstr "Da li može da isplaćuje, ko joj duguje i pod kojim uslovima radi."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.bankRunning.p1"
msgid "A bank keeps other players’ money and lends it. Its console says first whether it <b>can pay out</b>: its cash against what it owes the people who bank there."
msgstr "Banka čuva novac drugih igrača i od njega daje kredite. Njena konzola prvo kaže da li <b>može da isplaćuje</b>: njena gotovina naspram onoga što duguje ljudima koji u njoj drže novac."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.bankRunning.p2"
msgid "A bank that owes depositors more than it holds says so first. Winding a bank up is at the foot of More options and cannot be undone."
msgstr "Banka koja duguje deponentima više nego što ima to kaže prva. Zatvaranje banke je na dnu odeljka Još opcija i ne može da se poništi."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.bankRunning.title"
msgid "Running a bank"
msgstr "Vođenje banke"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.banking.line"
msgid "Keep money in a bank, borrow it, or run a bank yourself."
msgstr "Drži novac u banci, uzmi kredit ili sam vodi banku."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.banking.p1"
msgid "<b>Banks are run by players: you can put money in one, or borrow from one that lends to you.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Banke vode igrači: možeš da uložiš novac u banku ili da uzmeš kredit od banke koja ti ga daje.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.banking.p2"
msgid "To put money in: open Money, then Banks, and press Put money in on a bank. No bank pays interest on it. You take it out when the bank has the money to pay you."
msgstr "Da uložiš novac: otvori Novac, pa Banke, i pritisni Uloži novac kod neke banke. Nijedna banka na njega ne plaća kamatu. Novac podižeš kad banka ima čime da te isplati."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.banking.p3"
msgid "To borrow: open Money, then Loans. Each bank says how much it lends, its interest a year, for how long and how often you pay. The Borrow sheet says each payment, the day of the last, and what a missed payment does under that bank’s terms. One loan per bank at a time."
msgstr "Da uzmeš kredit: otvori Novac, pa Kredite. Svaka banka kaže koliko daje, kolika joj je godišnja kamata, na koliko dugo i koliko često plaćaš. Prozor Uzmi kredit pokazuje svaku ratu, dan poslednje rate i šta propuštena rata znači po uslovima te banke. Jedan kredit po banci odjednom."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.banking.p4"
msgid "To pay it back early: open the loan and press Repay, or Repay it all."
msgstr "Da vratiš kredit ranije: otvori kredit i pritisni Vrati ili Vrati sve."

#. {level} is a player level. {charter} is the charter fee, drawn as a coin amount. {capital} is the least capital, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.banking.p5"
msgid "From Level {level} you can found a bank: {charter} for the charter and at least {capital} of capital."
msgstr "Od nivoa {level} možeš da osnuješ banku: {charter} za taksu osnivanja i najmanje {capital} kapitala."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.banking.p6"
msgid "Words: Deposit: money you put in a bank. Interest: what a loan costs a year, as a part of what you borrow."
msgstr "Pojmovi: Depozit: novac koji uložiš u banku. Kamata: koliko kredit košta godišnje, kao deo onoga što pozajmiš."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.banking.title"
msgid "How do banks and loans work?"
msgstr "Kako rade banke i krediti?"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.answer"
msgid "Work your first shift, eat, train and choose where you live; Getting started in Now walks you through it."
msgstr "Odradi prvu smenu, jedi, treniraj i izaberi gde živiš; Prvi koraci na ekranu Sada vode te kroz to."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.line"
msgid "What to do first, step by step."
msgstr "Šta prvo da uradiš, korak po korak."

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English. {food} is a number of food items. {starterGrant} is the money a new citizen starts with, drawn as a coin amount. {newCountryGrant} is the money a newcomer starts with in a country that is still new, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.step1.how"
msgid "you are a citizen already, with {starterGrant} ({newCountryGrant} in a country that is still new), {food} food and a basic set of gear."
msgstr "već si građanin, sa {starterGrant} ({newCountryGrant} u državi koja je još nova), {food} hrane i osnovnom opremom."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.step1.to"
msgid "To begin"
msgstr "Za početak"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.step2.how"
msgid "press Work a shift on Home. Public works take anyone, with or without a job."
msgstr "pritisni Radi smenu na Početnoj. Javni radovi primaju svakoga, sa poslom ili bez njega."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.step2.to"
msgid "To earn"
msgstr "Da zaradiš"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.step3.how"
msgid "train once a day and finish today's goals; each level opens more of the game."
msgstr "treniraj jednom dnevno i završi današnje ciljeve; svaki nivo otvara više igre."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.step3.to"
msgid "To grow"
msgstr "Da napreduješ"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.step4.how"
msgid "open a province on the map and choose Live here once you stand in it."
msgstr "otvori oblast na mapi i izaberi Živi ovde kad se nađeš u njoj."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.step4.to"
msgid "To settle"
msgstr "Da se nastaniš"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.step5.how"
msgid "vote after a few days, trade on the Market, write for a paper, and fight when your country is at war."
msgstr "glasaj posle nekoliko dana, trguj na Tržištu, piši za novine i bori se kad je tvoja država u ratu."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.step5.to"
msgid "Later"
msgstr "Kasnije"

#. Everyday words a player might type into Help's search to find this page, separated by commas. Give the words people in your language would search with, and add others if you like. Keep the commas.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.synonyms"
msgid "new, start, begin, first, tutorial, guide, how to play"
msgstr "novo, početak, početi, pocetak, prvo, uputstvo, vodič, tutorijal, kako se igra, kako igrati"

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.title"
msgid "Your first hour"
msgstr "Tvoj prvi sat"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.word1.means"
msgid "The steps in Now that take you through your first day."
msgstr "Koraci na ekranu Sada koji te vode kroz prvi dan."

#. A word this page explains, shown in bold above its meaning.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.word1.term"
msgid "Getting started"
msgstr "Prvi koraci"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.word2.means"
msgid "What your experience adds up to; each one opens more of the game."
msgstr "Zbir tvog iskustva; svaki novi nivo otvara više igre."

#. A word this page explains, shown in bold above its meaning.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.basics.word2.term"
msgid "Level"
msgstr "Nivo"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chamber.line"
msgid "Members propose bills and vote on them."
msgstr "Članovi predlažu zakone i glasaju o njima."

#. {hours} is a number of hours.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chamber.p1"
msgid "<b>The chamber is the country’s elected assembly. Its members propose bills and vote on each for {hours} hours.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Skupština je izabrano telo države. Njeni članovi predlažu zakone i glasaju o svakom tokom {hours, plural, one {{hours} sata} few {{hours} sata} other {{hours} sati}}.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chamber.p2"
msgid "A bill passes with more yes than no votes. A change to the constitution needs two thirds. How each member voted is public."
msgstr "Predlog prolazi kad ima više glasova za nego protiv. Za izmenu ustava potrebne su dve trećine. Glas svakog člana je javan."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chamber.p3"
msgid "To follow a bill: Country, Politics, The chamber lists every bill, its tally and when its vote closes."
msgstr "Da pratiš predlog zakona: Država, Politika, Skupština navodi svaki predlog, stanje glasova i kad se glasanje zatvara."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chamber.p4"
msgid "To propose one: a member, or an office that may propose bills, uses Propose a bill on the same screen."
msgstr "Da predložiš zakon: član, ili funkcija koja sme da predlaže zakone, koristi Predloži zakon na istom ekranu."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chamber.p5"
msgid "Words: Member: somebody holding a seat in the chamber."
msgstr "Pojmovi: Član: neko ko drži mesto u Skupštini."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chamber.title"
msgid "How does the chamber work?"
msgstr "Kako radi Skupština?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chat.line"
msgid "Rooms, direct messages, and staying safe."
msgstr "Sobe, direktne poruke i bezbednost."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chat.p1"
msgid "<b>Chat is the rooms you are in and the people you write to.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Ćaskanje su sobe u kojima si i ljudi kojima pišeš.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chat.p2"
msgid "Your rooms: the whole world, your country, and every party, unit, company or battle you belong to. Press a room to open it."
msgstr "Tvoje sobe: ceo svet, tvoja država i svaka stranka, jedinica, firma ili bitka kojoj pripadaš. Pritisni sobu da je otvoriš."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chat.p3"
msgid "To write: type in the box and press Send. The world room may ask you to wait between messages, and Send counts it down. Press + to mention somebody, add an emoji or a sticker, or attach a picture."
msgstr "Da pišeš: ukucaj poruku u polje i pritisni Pošalji. Soba sveta može da traži da čekaš između poruka, a Pošalji odbrojava to vreme. Pritisni + da pomeneš nekoga, dodaš emodži ili nalepnicu ili priložiš sliku."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chat.p4"
msgid "To answer one message: open its ⋯ and press Reply. To write to one person, press Message on their page."
msgstr "Da odgovoriš na jednu poruku: otvori njeno ⋯ i pritisni Odgovori. Da pišeš jednoj osobi, pritisni Poruka na njenoj stranici."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.chat.title"
msgid "How does Chat work?"
msgstr "Kako radi Ćaskanje?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.citizenship.line"
msgid "Which country you belong to, and moving to another."
msgstr "Kojoj državi pripadaš i prelazak u drugu."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.citizenship.p1"
msgid "<b>You are a citizen of one country at a time. It is where you vote, run for office and join a party.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Građanin si samo jedne države odjednom. U njoj glasaš, kandiduješ se za funkcije i pristupaš stranci.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.citizenship.p2"
msgid "To change: open the other country’s People and apply. Some countries let everyone in at once; in others an office decides. The application says what moving would end for you."
msgstr "Da promeniš: otvori Ljudi u drugoj državi i podnesi zahtev. Neke države primaju sve odmah; u drugima odlučuje neka funkcija. Zahtev kaže šta bi ti prelazak okončao."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.citizenship.p3"
msgid "There is a wait between changes, and after moving you wait longer before you can vote or run. Your own dates are on the People screen."
msgstr "Između promena postoji čekanje, a posle prelaska čekaš duže pre nego što možeš da glasaš ili da se kandiduješ. Tvoji datumi su na ekranu Ljudi."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.citizenship.p4"
msgid "Words: Citizen: a member of a country."
msgstr "Pojmovi: Građanin: član jedne države."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.citizenship.title"
msgid "Citizenship, and how to change it"
msgstr "Državljanstvo i kako da ga promeniš"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.coins.line"
msgid "Frames, banners and name colours for how you look."
msgstr "Okviri, baneri i boje imena za tvoj izgled."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.coins.p1"
msgid "<b>Coins are a second currency, for how you look and how much room you have, never for an advantage.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Novčići su druga valuta, za tvoj izgled i za to koliko prostora imaš, nikad za prednost.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.coins.p2"
msgid "They are bought with real money once the store opens, and buying them is not open yet. They cannot be turned into CR."
msgstr "Kupuju se pravim novcem kad se Prodavnica otvori, a kupovina još nije otvorena. Ne mogu da se pretvore u CR."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.coins.p3"
msgid "To try something on: open it in the Store and press Try it on. Only you see it, nothing is bought, and it ends when you leave the Store."
msgstr "Da probaš nešto: otvori to u Prodavnici i pritisni Probaj. To vidiš samo ti, ništa se ne kupuje, a završava se kad napustiš Prodavnicu."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.coins.p4"
msgid "To wear what you own: open it and press Wear. A title you earned is worn from your public page."
msgstr "Da nosiš ono što imaš: otvori to i pritisni Nosi. Zarađena titula se nosi sa tvoje javne stranice."

#. {coins} is a number of Coins.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.coins.p5"
msgid "Supporter, once it is on sale: {coins} Coins a month, a badge and extra slots. The tip jar on Ko-fi buys nothing and changes nothing."
msgstr "Podržavalac, kad bude u prodaji: {coins} Novčića mesečno, značka i dodatna mesta. Kasica za napojnice na Ko-fi ništa ne kupuje i ništa ne menja."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.coins.p6"
msgid "Words: Coins: the Store’s currency. Supporter: a monthly subscription for looks and room."
msgstr "Pojmovi: Novčići: valuta Prodavnice. Podržavalac: mesečna pretplata za izgled i prostor."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.coins.title"
msgid "What are Coins?"
msgstr "Šta su Novčići?"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.company.h1"
msgid "Words"
msgstr "Pojmovi"

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.company.li1"
msgid "<b>To make something:</b> open a site. It is a building in a province of your company’s country. The price shown is the whole price: the building and the goods bought for it."
msgstr "<b>Da nešto proizvedeš:</b> otvori pogon. To je zgrada u nekoj oblasti države tvoje firme. Prikazana cena je cela cena: zgrada i roba kupljena za nju."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.company.li2"
msgid "<b>To get it working:</b> advertise for people under People. Both sides are held for 24 hours once somebody is hired."
msgstr "<b>Da pokreneš rad:</b> objavi oglas za ljude pod Ljudi. Obe strane su vezane 24 sata čim firma nekoga primi."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.company.li3"
msgid "<b>To sell what it makes:</b> Trade and stock opens the Market as the company."
msgstr "<b>Da prodaš ono što proizvodi:</b> Trgovina i zalihe otvara Tržište u ime firme."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.company.li4"
msgid "<b>To pay its owners:</b> Money. It keeps two weeks of wages and what it owes."
msgstr "<b>Da isplatiš vlasnike:</b> Novac. Firma zadržava plate za dve nedelje i ono što duguje."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.company.line"
msgid "Sites, people, money and stock, from one screen."
msgstr "Pogoni, ljudi, novac i zalihe, sa jednog ekrana."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.company.p1"
msgid "Open it from You: its first screen says what waits on you, what is wrong, and what runs by itself."
msgstr "Otvori je iz odeljka Ti: njen prvi ekran kaže šta čeka tebe, šta nije u redu i šta radi samo od sebe."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.company.p2"
msgid "<b>Site:</b> a building where your company makes things. <b>Stock:</b> what its sites hold. <b>Payout:</b> money paid to its owners by their shares."
msgstr "<b>Pogon:</b> zgrada u kojoj tvoja firma proizvodi. <b>Zalihe:</b> ono što njeni pogoni drže. <b>Isplata:</b> novac koji se vlasnicima isplaćuje prema njihovim akcijama."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.company.title"
msgid "How do I run a company?"
msgstr "Kako da vodim firmu?"

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyFounding.li1"
msgid "<b>Alone:</b> you pay all of it and own all of it."
msgstr "<b>Sam:</b> ti plaćaš sve i sve je tvoje."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label. {partners} is a number of citizens. {hours} is a number of hours.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyFounding.li2"
msgid "<b>With partners:</b> up to {partners} citizens of its country put money in and own shares by what they put in. You send them a link. If it is not all in within {hours} hours, everyone’s money goes back."
msgstr "<b>Sa partnerima:</b> do {partners} građana njene države ulaže novac i dobija akcije srazmerno ulogu. Šalješ im link. Ako sve ne stigne u roku od {hours, plural, one {{hours} sata} few {{hours} sata} other {{hours} sati}}, novac svih se vraća."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyFounding.li3"
msgid "<b>Where it is registered is for good:</b> it can only build in that country. The fee goes to the treasury of whoever holds the province."
msgstr "<b>Mesto registracije je zauvek:</b> firma može da gradi samo u toj državi. Taksa ide u državnu kasu one države koja drži oblast."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyFounding.line"
msgid "Alone or with partners, and what is for good."
msgstr "Sam ili sa partnerima, i šta je zauvek."

#. {level} is a player level. {charter} is the fee to found a company, drawn as a coin amount. {startMoney} is the least start money a company needs, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyFounding.p1"
msgid "From level {level} you can found a company from You › Start something. It takes a {charter} fee and at least {startMoney} of start money, which becomes the company’s."
msgstr "Od nivoa {level} možeš da osnuješ firmu u odeljku Ti › Pokreni nešto. Potrebna je taksa od {charter} i najmanje {startMoney} početnog novca, koji postaje novac firme."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyFounding.p2"
msgid "Once it exists, open its first site: until then it can make and hire nothing."
msgstr "Kad firma postoji, otvori njen prvi pogon: do tada ne može ništa da proizvodi ni da zapošljava."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyFounding.title"
msgid "How do I start a company?"
msgstr "Kako da osnujem firmu?"

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyHiring.li1"
msgid "<b>Advertise for people:</b> say how many, from which level, and the pay for a short shift. The screen says what a full shift then pays, and warns you when you would pay more than a shift makes."
msgstr "<b>Objavi oglas za ljude:</b> reci koliko ljudi, od kog nivoa i platu za kratku smenu. Ekran kaže koliko tada plaća puna smena i upozorava te kad je plata veća od onoga što smena donosi."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyHiring.li2"
msgid "<b>Ask me first</b> lets you answer each person. <b>Hire anyone who qualifies</b> takes them at once."
msgstr "<b>Prvo pitaj mene</b> ti daje da odgovoriš svakoj osobi. <b>Primi svakoga ko ispunjava uslove</b> prima ih odmah."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label. {hours} is a number of hours.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyHiring.li3"
msgid "<b>Answering:</b> Hire or Refuse. Once somebody is hired, both sides are held for {hours} hours."
msgstr "<b>Odgovor:</b> Primi ili Odbij. Čim firma nekoga primi, obe strane su vezane na {hours, plural, one {{hours} sat} few {{hours} sata} other {{hours} sati}}."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyHiring.li4"
msgid "<b>Wages</b> are paid from the company’s money each day; the console says how many days it has in hand."
msgstr "<b>Plate</b> se isplaćuju iz novca firme svakog dana; konzola kaže za koliko dana firma ima novca unapred."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyHiring.line"
msgid "Adverts, applicants, pay, and handing hiring over."
msgstr "Oglasi, kandidati, plata i prepuštanje zapošljavanja."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyHiring.p1"
msgid "A company hires from its People once it has a site that is open."
msgstr "Firma prima ljude preko odeljka Ljudi čim ima pogon koji je otvoren."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyHiring.p2"
msgid "Under More options you can let idle workers go after a number of days, or hand hiring over to someone you trust, with a job title."
msgstr "U odeljku Još opcija možeš da otpustiš radnike koji ne rade posle određenog broja dana ili da prepustiš zapošljavanje nekome kome veruješ, uz naziv posla."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companyHiring.title"
msgid "How do I hire people?"
msgstr "Kako da zaposlim ljude?"

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companySite.li1"
msgid "<b>What it makes:</b> each choice shows the whole price of its cheapest place, what a site makes a day and what that sells for today."
msgstr "<b>Šta proizvodi:</b> svaki izbor pokazuje celu cenu najjeftinijeg mesta za njega, koliko pogon proizvede za dan i za koliko se to danas prodaje."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companySite.li2"
msgid "<b>Where:</b> a province of your company’s own country, with its industry level and the room left. A province another country holds is shown, and cannot be chosen."
msgstr "<b>Gde:</b> oblast države tvoje firme, sa njenim industrijskim nivoom i preostalim prostorom. Oblast koju drži druga država se prikazuje, ali ne može da se izabere."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companySite.li3"
msgid "<b>How big:</b> a bigger site has more places to work. You can make it bigger later; it stops for a few hours then."
msgstr "<b>Koliki:</b> veći pogon ima više radnih mesta. Možeš kasnije da ga povećaš; tada staje na nekoliko sati."

#. One item of a list; the bold start is a short label.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companySite.li4"
msgid "<b>The price:</b> the building and the goods it needs, bought on the Market for the company. Nothing more is spent than the price you were shown."
msgstr "<b>Cena:</b> zgrada i roba koja joj treba, kupljena na Tržištu za firmu. Ne troši se ništa više od cene koja ti je prikazana."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companySite.line"
msgid "What it makes, where, how big, and what it costs."
msgstr "Šta proizvodi, gde, koliki je i koliko košta."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companySite.p1"
msgid "A site is a building where your company makes one thing. Open one from your company’s Sites."
msgstr "Pogon je zgrada u kojoj tvoja firma proizvodi jednu stvar. Otvori ga u odeljku Pogoni svoje firme."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companySite.p2"
msgid "A site works once it has people, or an automation line. Pulling one down is at the foot of the site’s More options."
msgstr "Pogon radi čim ima ljude ili automatsku liniju. Rušenje pogona je na dnu odeljka Još opcija tog pogona."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.companySite.title"
msgid "How do I open a site?"
msgstr "Kako da otvorim pogon?"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.country.h1"
msgid "Voting and running for office"
msgstr "Glasanje i kandidovanje za funkcije"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.country.h2"
msgid "Laws and taxes"
msgstr "Zakoni i porezi"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.country.h3"
msgid "Changing citizenship and parties"
msgstr "Promena državljanstva i stranke"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.country.line"
msgid "Citizenship, elections, laws and taxes."
msgstr "Državljanstvo, izbori, zakoni i porezi."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.country.p1"
msgid "Every country is run by its players. Citizens elect the people who make the laws, set the taxes and can declare war."
msgstr "Svaku državu vode njeni igrači. Građani biraju ljude koji donose zakone, određuju poreze i mogu da objave rat."

#. The first three numbers are days of citizenship: {originalVote} before voting, {originalAssembly} before running for the assembly, {originalHeadOfState} before running for head of state, for a citizen who never changed country. {migrantVote}, {migrantAssembly} and {migrantHeadOfState} are the same three waits, in days, for a citizen who moved from another country.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.country.p2"
msgid "Both depend on how many days you have been a citizen of that country. If you have never changed citizenship, you can vote after {originalVote} days, run for the assembly after {originalAssembly} and for head of state after {originalHeadOfState}. If you moved from another country it is {migrantVote}, {migrantAssembly} and {migrantHeadOfState} days. The Country screen shows your own dates."
msgstr "Oba prava zavise od toga koliko dana si građanin te države. Ako od početka pripadaš ovoj državi, možeš da glasaš posle {originalVote} dana, da se kandiduješ za Skupštinu posle {originalAssembly} i za šefa države posle {originalHeadOfState}. Ako dolaziš iz druge države, to je {migrantVote}, {migrantAssembly} i {migrantHeadOfState} dana. Ekran Država prikazuje tvoje datume."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.country.p3"
msgid "While a country is new there is no wait at all: see A new country."
msgstr "Dok je država nova, nema nikakvog čekanja: pogledaj Nova država."

#. {nominationDays} is a number of days. {votingDays} is a number of days.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.country.p4"
msgid "An election has {nominationDays} day for candidates to run, then {votingDays} day of voting, the first election for an office too. If nobody runs against you, you take the seat when entries close, with no vote. A chamber is elected by place, so for a seat in it that means nobody else running where you live. An office the chamber chooses, such as a prime minister, is the exception: anybody may run for it, and the chamber’s members always vote, even on one name."
msgstr "Izbori imaju {nominationDays, plural, one {{nominationDays} dan} few {{nominationDays} dana} other {{nominationDays} dana}} za prijavu kandidata, a zatim {votingDays, plural, one {{votingDays} dan} few {{votingDays} dana} other {{votingDays} dana}} glasanja; isto važi i za prve izbore za neku funkciju. Ako se niko ne kandiduje protiv tebe, dobijaš mesto kad se prijave zatvore, bez glasanja. Skupština se bira po oblastima, pa za mesto u njoj to znači da se u tvojoj oblasti niko drugi ne kandiduje. Funkcija koju bira Skupština, na primer premijer, je izuzetak: svako može da se kandiduje za nju, a članovi Skupštine uvek glasaju, čak i kad postoji samo jedno ime."

#. {hours} is a number of hours.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.country.p5"
msgid "Members of the assembly propose laws and vote on them for {hours} hours. A president or prime minister may propose laws too, and votes on them only with a seat of their own. A law passes with more yes than no votes; a change to the constitution needs two thirds. Taxes are set this way, so they differ from country to country: see your country’s Money room."
msgstr "Članovi Skupštine predlažu zakone i glasaju o njima tokom {hours, plural, one {{hours} sata} few {{hours} sata} other {{hours} sati}}. I predsednik ili premijer mogu da predlažu zakone, a glasaju o njima samo ako imaju sopstveno mesto. Zakon prolazi kad ima više glasova za nego protiv; za izmenu ustava potrebne su dve trećine. Porezi se određuju na ovaj način, pa se razlikuju od države do države: pogledaj odeljak Novac svoje države."

#. {level} is a player level. {fee} is the fee to found a party, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.country.p6"
msgid "You can apply to become a citizen of another country. Some countries accept everyone at once, others have an official decide. There is a wait between changes. From level {level} you can found a political party for {fee}."
msgstr "Možeš da se prijaviš za državljanstvo druge države. Neke države primaju sve odmah, a u drugima odlučuje neko na funkciji. Između promena postoji čekanje. Od nivoa {level} možeš da osnuješ političku stranku za {fee}."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.country.title"
msgid "Your country and how to take part"
msgstr "Tvoja država i kako da učestvuješ"

