msgctxt "help.foundingEra.h1"
msgid "What is different"
msgstr "Šta je drugačije"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.foundingEra.h2"
msgid "Before the first government"
msgstr "Pre prve vlade"

#. A heading inside the page.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.foundingEra.h3"
msgid "Running unopposed"
msgstr "Kandidovanje bez protivkandidata"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.foundingEra.line"
msgid "Why the first days in a country are easier."
msgstr "Zašto su prvi dani u državi lakši."

#. {companies} is a number of companies. {days} is a number of days.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.foundingEra.p1"
msgid "A country is new from the day its first citizen arrives until players own {companies} companies there, or for {days} days, whichever comes first. The Country screen says when yours is."
msgstr "Država je nova od dana kad stigne njen prvi građanin, dok igrači tamo ne poseduju {companies, plural, one {{companies} firmu} few {{companies} firme} other {{companies} firmi}}, ili {days, plural, one {{days} dan} few {{days} dana} other {{days} dana}}, šta god nastupi prvo. Ekran Država kaže dokle to traje za tvoju državu."

#. {newCountryGrant} is the money a newcomer starts with in a country that is still new, drawn as a coin amount. {starterGrant} is the money a new citizen starts with, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.foundingEra.p2"
msgid "Newcomers here start with {newCountryGrant} instead of {starterGrant}, and founding a company here needs no waiting, whoever founds it."
msgstr "Novi građani ovde počinju sa {newCountryGrant} umesto {starterGrant}, a osnivanje firme ovde ne zahteva čekanje, ko god je osniva."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.foundingEra.p3"
msgid "If you started playing in that country, you can vote and run for office at once, with no waiting. Somebody who moves there from another country waits the usual time for a newcomer from abroad, new country or not. When the country stops being new, the usual waits come back for everybody, counted from the day each person arrived: somebody who arrived yesterday waits out the rest of theirs, and the Country screen gives them the day."
msgstr "Ako igru počneš u toj državi, možeš odmah da glasaš i da se kandiduješ, bez čekanja. Ko se tamo preseli iz druge države, čeka uobičajeno vreme za pridošlicu iz inostranstva, bilo da je država nova ili ne. Kad država prestane da bude nova, uobičajena čekanja se vraćaju za sve, računajući od dana dolaska svake osobe: osoba čiji je dolazak bio juče čeka ostatak svog roka, a ekran Država joj daje dan."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.foundingEra.p4"
msgid "Until somebody is elected, nobody governs. What runs on its own keeps running, and nobody can pass a law, spend from the treasury or declare war. A monarchy with nobody on its throne holds a first election for it among its citizens, and whoever wins holds it for life."
msgstr "Dok se neko ne izabere, niko ne vlada. Ono što radi samo od sebe nastavlja da radi, a niko ne može da donese zakon, da troši iz državne kase ni da objavi rat. Monarhija bez nikoga na prestolu održava prve izbore za njega među svojim građanima, a ko pobedi, drži ga doživotno."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.foundingEra.p5"
msgid "If nobody runs against you, there is nothing to vote on: when entries close, you take the seat. So if you are the only one running for President, you become President. A chamber is elected by place, so for a seat in it that means nobody else running where you live. A name on a ballot cannot be taken off, and the Run button says so before you press it. An office the chamber chooses is never taken unopposed: its members vote even when one person runs."
msgstr "Ako se niko ne kandiduje protiv tebe, nema o čemu da se glasa: kad se prijave zatvore, dobijaš mesto. Dakle, ako si jedini kandidat za predsednika, postaješ predsednik. Skupština se bira po oblastima, pa za mesto u njoj to znači da se u tvojoj oblasti niko drugi ne kandiduje. Ime sa listića ne može da se skine, a dugme Kandiduj se to kaže pre nego što ga pritisneš. Funkcija koju bira Skupština nikad se ne dobija bez protivkandidata: njeni članovi glasaju čak i kad se kandiduje jedna osoba."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.foundingEra.title"
msgid "A new country"
msgstr "Nova država"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.gazette.line"
msgid "Where a government speaks for its country."
msgstr "Gde vlada govori u ime svoje države."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.gazette.p1"
msgid "<b>It is where a government speaks for its country.</b>"
msgstr "<b>To je mesto gde vlada govori u ime svoje države.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.gazette.p2"
msgid "To read it: its notices appear in News under Your country, marked Official notice, and its front page lists all of them and the offices that write there. Every citizen of the country gets its notices without following it."
msgstr "Da ga čitaš: njegova obaveštenja se pojavljuju u Vestima pod Tvoja država, označena kao Službeno obaveštenje, a njegova naslovna strana navodi sva obaveštenja i funkcije koje tamo pišu. Svaki građanin države dobija njegova obaveštenja i bez praćenja."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.gazette.p3"
msgid "To write a notice: hold an office that writes there, then press Write a notice on its front page. A notice costs nothing to print, and you write it while you hold the office."
msgstr "Da napišeš obaveštenje: drži funkciju koja tamo piše, pa pritisni Napiši obaveštenje na njegovoj naslovnoj strani. Štampanje obaveštenja ne košta ništa, a pišeš ga dok držiš funkciju."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.gazette.title"
msgid "What is the Official Gazette?"
msgstr "Šta je Službeni glasnik?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.giving.line"
msgid "Give goods to a person, or offer them for a price."
msgstr "Daj robu osobi ili je ponudi za cenu."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.giving.p1"
msgid "<b>Open their page and press Give or sell, or start from a good in your Inventory.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Otvori njenu stranicu i pritisni Daj ili prodaj, ili kreni od neke robe u svom inventaru.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.giving.p2"
msgid "To give: choose Give, what and how many, and press Give. To sell: choose Sell and set a price for all of it, which they pay when they accept."
msgstr "Da daš: izaberi Daj, šta i koliko, i pritisni Daj. Da prodaš: izaberi Prodaj i odredi cenu za sve, koju osoba plaća kad prihvati."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.giving.p3"
msgid "What you send is held for them at once, and they are told. If they say no, or do not answer in time, it all comes back to you. You can withdraw the offer before they answer."
msgstr "Ono što šalješ odmah se zadržava za osobu, a ona dobija obaveštenje. Ako odbije ili ne odgovori na vreme, sve se vraća tebi. Ponudu možeš da povučeš pre nego što osoba odgovori."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.giving.p4"
msgid "Goods given or sold to a person pay no freight and no import tax, wherever they are."
msgstr "Roba data ili prodata osobi ne plaća prevoz ni carinu, gde god da se nalazi."

#. {hours} is a number of hours.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.giving.p5"
msgid "For your first {hours} hours, your starting gear and early rewards cannot be sold or given away. The sheet says the day you can."
msgstr "Tokom prvih {hours, plural, one {{hours} sata} few {{hours} sata} other {{hours} sati}} tvoja početna oprema i rane nagrade ne mogu da se prodaju ni poklone. Prozor kaže od kog dana možeš."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.giving.p6"
msgid "Words: Held: kept for them until they answer."
msgstr "Pojmovi: Zadržano: sačuvano za osobu dok ne odgovori."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.giving.title"
msgid "How do I give or sell to someone?"
msgstr "Kako da nekome dam ili prodam?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.givingOrders.line"
msgid "Telling your side where to fight."
msgstr "Poručivanje svojoj strani gde da se bori."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.givingOrders.p1"
msgid "An order is given on a battle, in the name of a unit (by its commander or an officer) or of a country (by whoever holds that power). It says what to do, how urgent it is and when it ends."
msgstr "Naređenje se izdaje za bitku, u ime jedinice (od njenog komandanta ili oficira) ili države (od onoga ko drži to ovlašćenje). Kaže šta treba uraditi, koliko je hitno i kada se završava."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.givingOrders.p2"
msgid "Everybody fighting for your side in that battle reads it right above the Fight buttons, and the unit’s soldiers see it first in Now. Other orders keep standing beside it. Whoever gave an order can take it back while it stands, and it ends by itself when its time is up or its battle is decided."
msgstr "Svako ko se u toj bitki bori za tvoju stranu čita ga odmah iznad dugmadi Bori se, a vojnici jedinice ga prvo vide u Sada. Druga naređenja i dalje stoje pored njega. Onaj ko izda naređenje može da ga povuče dok važi, a ono se završava samo kad mu istekne vreme ili kad se bitka odluči."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.givingOrders.title"
msgid "Giving orders"
msgstr "Izdavanje naređenja"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.inventory.line"
msgid "Gear, food, goods and cases."
msgstr "Oprema, hrana, roba i kutije."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.inventory.p1"
msgid "<b>Inventory holds what you wear, your goods and your cases. What a company or a unit you run holds is on its own page.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Inventar drži ono što nosiš, tvoju robu i tvoje kutije. Ono što drži firma ili jedinica kojom upravljaš je na njenoj stranici.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.inventory.p2"
msgid "To wear something: press Wear on a piece. You wear five: a weapon, a helmet, body armor, legwear and boots. Power is how hard you hit, Protection how much of a hit your armor takes, and Mobility how light you move."
msgstr "Da nešto nosiš: pritisni Nosi na komadu opreme. Nosiš pet komada: oružje, šlem, oklop, pantalone i čizme. Snaga je koliko jako udaraš, Zaštita koliko od udarca preuzima tvoj oklop, a Pokretljivost koliko lako se krećeš."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.inventory.p3"
msgid "To mend a piece: open it and press Repair, which costs Scrap. A piece at nothing is broken and stops counting in a fight. Only a broken piece can be broken up for Scrap or retired."
msgstr "Da popraviš komad: otvori ga i pritisni Popravi, što košta otpad. Komad na nuli je pokvaren i prestaje da se računa u borbi. Samo pokvaren komad može da se rastavi na otpad ili povuče iz upotrebe."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.inventory.p4"
msgid "To use goods: open one to sell it, give it to someone, or, for food, eat it. To open a case: press Open one, or Open all."
msgstr "Da koristiš robu: otvori je da je prodaš, daš nekome ili, ako je hrana, pojedeš. Da otvoriš kutiju: pritisni Otvori jednu kutiju ili Otvori sve."

#. {common} is a percentage, printed without the percent sign. {uncommon} is a percentage, printed without the percent sign. {rare} is a percentage, printed without the percent sign. {epic} is a percentage, printed without the percent sign. {legendary} is a percentage, printed without the percent sign.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.inventory.p5"
msgid "Gear made in a factory comes out rarer than gear from a case: {common}% Common, {uncommon}% Uncommon, {rare}% Rare, {epic}% Epic and {legendary}% Legendary."
msgstr "Oprema napravljena u fabrici ispada ređa od opreme iz kutije: {common}% običnih, {uncommon}% neobičnih, {rare}% retkih, {epic}% epskih i {legendary}% legendarnih."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.inventory.p6"
msgid "Words: Scrap: what gear is mended with. Condition: how worn a piece is, out of the best it can still reach."
msgstr "Pojmovi: Otpad: čime se oprema popravlja. Stanje: koliko je komad pohaban, u odnosu na najbolje do čega još može da dođe."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.inventory.title"
msgid "What do I own, and how do I use it?"
msgstr "Šta posedujem i kako to da koristim?"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.after"
msgid "You hold one job at a time. Taking one withdraws your other applications."
msgstr "Imaš jedan posao odjednom. Prihvatanje jednog povlači tvoje ostale prijave."

#. {hours} is a number of hours.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.answer"
msgid "Apply for a job and work its shifts; for {hours} hours after you are hired, neither you nor the company can end it."
msgstr "Prijavi se za posao i radi njegove smene; tokom {hours, plural, one {{hours} sata} few {{hours} sata} other {{hours} sati}} nakon što te firma primi, ni ti ni firma ne možete da ga prekinete."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.line"
msgid "Applying, working and leaving."
msgstr "Prijava, rad i odlazak."

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.step1.how"
msgid "open Ways to earn, then Jobs. Some jobs hire you at once; others send your application to the company, which says yes or no."
msgstr "otvori Načine zarade, pa Poslove. Neki poslovi te primaju odmah; drugi šalju tvoju prijavu firmi, koja kaže da ili ne."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.step1.to"
msgid "To apply"
msgstr "Da se prijaviš"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.step2.how"
msgid "each job says what a full and a short shift pay you after tax."
msgstr "svaki posao kaže koliko ti plaćaju puna i kratka smena posle poreza."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.step2.to"
msgid "To compare"
msgstr "Da uporediš"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.step3.how"
msgid "your applications are above the board, each with Withdraw it."
msgstr "tvoje prijave su iznad table, svaka sa dugmetom Povuci prijavu."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.step3.to"
msgid "To change your mind"
msgstr "Da se predomisliš"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.step4.how"
msgid "press Leave this job on your job's card, once your hours are up."
msgstr "pritisni Napusti ovaj posao na kartici svog posla, kad ti istekne obavezni rok."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.step4.to"
msgid "To leave"
msgstr "Da odeš"

#. Everyday words a player might type into Help's search to find this page, separated by commas. Give the words people in your language would search with, and add others if you like. Keep the commas.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.synonyms"
msgid "job, apply, hire, employer, quit, leave, resign"
msgstr "posao, poslovi, prijava, prijavi se, zaposlenje, poslodavac, otkaz, napusti, ostavka"

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.title"
msgid "How do jobs work?"
msgstr "Kako rade poslovi?"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.word1.means"
msgid "What a shift pays before tax."
msgstr "Koliko smena plaća pre poreza."

#. A word this page explains, shown in bold above its meaning.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.word1.term"
msgid "Wage"
msgstr "Plata"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.word2.means"
msgid "A company your country owns; it hires anyone at its wage."
msgstr "Firma koju poseduje tvoja država; prima svakoga uz svoju platu."

#. A word this page explains, shown in bold above its meaning.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.jobs.word2.term"
msgid "State company"
msgstr "Državna firma"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.letters.line"
msgid "What readers send a piece and its writer."
msgstr "Šta čitaoci šalju članku i njegovom novinaru."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.letters.p1"
msgid "<b>Under every piece, readers write letters and can thank the writer with a tip.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Ispod svakog članka čitaoci pišu pisma i mogu da zahvale novinaru napojnicom.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.letters.p2"
msgid "To write a letter: type it in the box under the piece and post it. Letters are public, with your name and country. You can withdraw your own letter from its ⋯."
msgstr "Da napišeš pismo: ukucaj ga u polje ispod članka i objavi. Pisma su javna, sa tvojim imenom i državom. Svoje pismo možeš da povučeš iz njegovog ⋯."

#. {paperShare} is a percentage, printed without the percent sign. {minimumTip} is the smallest tip, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.letters.p3"
msgid "To thank the writer: press Thank and choose an amount, from {minimumTip}. The writer keeps most of it and the paper keeps the rest ({paperShare}% unless its owner changes it). You thank a writer once for each piece."
msgstr "Da zahvališ novinaru: pritisni Zahvali se i izaberi iznos, od {minimumTip}. Novinar zadržava većinu, a novine ostatak ({paperShare}% osim ako vlasnik to ne promeni). Novinaru se zahvaljuješ jednom za svaki članak."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.letters.p4"
msgid "To say what you thought: Good piece or Not for me. To report a letter or a piece, open its ⋯."
msgstr "Da kažeš šta misliš: Dobar članak ili Nije za mene. Da prijaviš pismo ili članak, otvori njegovo ⋯."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.letters.title"
msgid "How do letters and tips work?"
msgstr "Kako rade pisma i napojnice?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.market.line"
msgid "Buying, selling, and what a trade costs."
msgstr "Kupovina, prodaja i koliko košta trgovina."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.market.p1"
msgid "<b>Every good has a page in the Market, with its price delivered to where you are and one button that buys or sells.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Svaka roba ima stranicu na Tržištu, sa cenom sa isporukom do mesta gde si i jednim dugmetom koje kupuje ili prodaje.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.market.p2"
msgid "To buy: open the good, choose Buy and how many, and press the button. It shows the total, and that is what you pay. The cheapest offers are taken first."
msgstr "Da kupiš: otvori robu, izaberi Kupi i koliko, pa pritisni dugme. Ono pokazuje ukupan iznos, i to plaćaš. Prvo se uzimaju najjeftinije ponude."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.market.p3"
msgid "To sell: choose Sell. Sell now sells to the buyers paying most; when nobody is buying, set your own price."
msgstr "Da prodaš: izaberi Prodaj. Prodaj odmah prodaje kupcima koji plaćaju najviše; kad niko ne kupuje, postavi svoju cenu."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.market.p4"
msgid "To set your own price: press Set your own price. An offer to buy sets its money aside and a listing holds your goods, until one is taken."
msgstr "Da postaviš svoju cenu: pritisni Postavi svoju cenu. Ponuda za kupovinu odvaja svoj novac, a oglas drži tvoju robu, dok je neko ne prihvati."

#. {percent} is a percentage, printed without the percent sign. {amount} is the size of a trade that asks first, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.market.p5"
msgid "The total is the price, freight by weight and distance, a fee of {percent}% paid to the country the goods are delivered to, and an import tax on goods from another country. A trade of {amount} or more asks you first."
msgstr "Ukupan iznos čine cena, prevoz prema težini i udaljenosti, naknada od {percent}% koja ide državi u koju se roba isporučuje i carina na robu iz druge države. Trgovina od {amount} ili više pita te prvo."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.market.p6"
msgid "Until a country’s players make enough, the game’s shop sells food, construction materials, industrial components and fuel in its capital, at a price anyone who makes it can sell for less."
msgstr "Dok igrači jedne države ne proizvedu dovoljno, igra sama prodaje hranu, građevinski materijal, industrijske komponente i gorivo u njenom glavnom gradu, po ceni koju svako ko to proizvodi može da ponudi jeftinije."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.market.p7"
msgid "Words: Delivered: the price with every charge, to where you are. Bid: an offer to buy at your own price."
msgstr "Pojmovi: Sa isporukom: cena sa svim troškovima, do mesta gde si. Ponuda za kupovinu: ponuda da kupiš po svojoj ceni."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.market.title"
msgid "How do I buy and sell?"
msgstr "Kako da kupujem i prodajem?"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.answer"
msgid "Read the report, decide it within 24 hours, and check the words the player will read before you send them."
msgstr "Pročitaj prijavu, odluči o njoj u roku od 24 sata i proveri reči koje će igrač pročitati pre nego što ih pošalješ."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.line"
msgid "For staff: the queue, a decision, and an appeal."
msgstr "Za osoblje: red čekanja, odluka i žalba."

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.step1.how"
msgid "open the staff console: reports are oldest first, and one waiting more than 24 hours says Late."
msgstr "otvori konzolu osoblja: prijave idu od najstarije, a ona koja čeka duže od 24 sata nosi oznaku Kasni."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.step1.to"
msgid "To see what waits"
msgstr "Da vidiš šta čeka"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.step2.how"
msgid "open a report, press Decide, and choose what it stops and for how long."
msgstr "otvori prijavu, pritisni Odluči i izaberi šta se zabranjuje i na koliko dugo."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.step2.to"
msgid "To decide"
msgstr "Da odlučiš"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.step3.how"
msgid "the question shows the player's sentence, who is told, and that they may appeal."
msgstr "pitanje prikazuje igračevu kaznu, ko dobija obaveštenje i da igrač može da uloži žalbu."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.step3.to"
msgid "To check the words"
msgstr "Da proveriš reči"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.step4.how"
msgid "press Nothing was wrong. Close it."
msgstr "pritisni Ništa nije bilo sporno. Zatvori."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.step4.to"
msgid "To close one with nothing wrong"
msgstr "Da zatvoriš prijavu u kojoj nije bilo ničeg spornog"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.step5.how"
msgid "a moderator who did not decide it reads it, and presses Lift it or Keep it."
msgstr "žalbu čita moderator koji nije autor odluke i pritiska Ukini ili Zadrži."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.step5.to"
msgid "To answer an appeal"
msgstr "Da odgovoriš na žalbu"

#. Everyday words a player might type into Help's search to find this page, separated by commas. Give the words people in your language would search with, and add others if you like. Keep the commas.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.synonyms"
msgid "report, sanction, moderate, moderation, appeal, staff"
msgstr "prijava, prijave, kazna, sankcija, moderacija, moderator, žalba, osoblje"

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.title"
msgid "Deciding a report"
msgstr "Odlučivanje o prijavi"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moderation.word1.means"
