#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.money.line"
msgid "CR, what you earn and spend, and where it went."
msgstr "CR, šta zarađuješ i trošiš i kuda je otišlo."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.money.p1"
msgid "<b>CR is the money of the world: you earn it, spend it and keep it in your wallet, and every movement is in your Records.</b>"
msgstr "<b>CR je novac sveta: zarađuješ ga, trošiš i čuvaš u novčaniku, a svaki promet je u tvojim Zapisima.</b>"

#. {starterGrant} is the money a new citizen starts with, drawn as a coin amount. {newCountryGrant} is the money a newcomer starts with in a country that is still new, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.money.p2"
msgid "To earn it: work a shift for a wage, sell on the Market, or take tips for what you write. New citizens start with {starterGrant} ({newCountryGrant} in a country that is still new)."
msgstr "Da ga zaradiš: odradi smenu za platu, prodaj na Tržištu ili primaj napojnice za ono što pišeš. Novi građani počinju sa {starterGrant} ({newCountryGrant} u državi koja je još nova)."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.money.p3"
msgid "To spend it: buy goods, travel, or start a company, a paper or a bank. An offer to buy sets its money aside: it is still yours, but you cannot spend it until the offer fills or you take it back."
msgstr "Da ga potrošiš: kupuj robu, putuj ili osnuj firmu, novine ili banku. Ponuda za kupovinu odvaja svoj novac: i dalje je tvoj, ali ne možeš da ga potrošiš dok se ponuda ne ispuni ili je ne povučeš."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.money.p4"
msgid "To see where it went: open Records at the foot of Money, and choose Earned, Spent, Banks and loans or Trades."
msgstr "Da vidiš kuda je otišao: otvori Zapise na dnu odeljka Novac i izaberi Zarađeno, Potrošeno, Banke i krediti ili Trgovina."

#. {hours} is a number of hours.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.money.p5"
msgid "Your country sets its taxes by law, and a new rate starts {hours} hours after the law passes. Its rates are under Country, Economy."
msgstr "Tvoja država određuje poreze zakonom, a nova stopa počinje {hours, plural, one {{hours} sat} few {{hours} sata} other {{hours} sati}} nakon što zakon prođe. Stope su u odeljku Država, Ekonomija."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.money.p6"
msgid "Words: CR: credits, the game’s money. Set aside: held by an offer to buy, and still yours."
msgstr "Pojmovi: CR: krediti, novac igre. Odvojeno: zadržano ponudom za kupovinu, a i dalje tvoje."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.money.title"
msgid "How does money work?"
msgstr "Kako radi novac?"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.after"
msgid "Old links still work: they open the place where the thing lives now."
msgstr "Stari linkovi i dalje rade: otvaraju mesto gde se ta stvar sada nalazi."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.answer"
msgid "Everything now lives in six places: Home, Market, News, Chat, Country and You. Each place you knew before is inside one of them."
msgstr "Sve je sada na šest mesta: Početna, Tržište, Vesti, Ćaskanje, Država i Ti. Svako mesto koje ti je bilo poznato od ranije nalazi se u jednom od njih."

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.line"
msgid "Where Today, Work, Press, Banking and the Menu went."
msgstr "Kuda su otišli Danas, Posao, Štampa, Bankarstvo i Meni."

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.step1.how"
msgid "press Home. Now and Today hold your next steps, your shift, training and eating. Jobs is under Find a job."
msgstr "pritisni Početna. Sada i Danas drže tvoje sledeće korake, tvoju smenu, trening i jelo. Poslovi su pod Nađi posao."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.step1.to"
msgid "To find Today and Work"
msgstr "Da nađeš Danas i Posao"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.step2.how"
msgid "press News: your country's papers, the world's, and the ones you follow."
msgstr "pritisni Vesti: novine tvoje države, sveta i one koje pratiš."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.step2.to"
msgid "To find Press"
msgstr "Da nađeš Štampu"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.step3.how"
msgid "press You, then Money: your accounts, loans and shares. A bank you run is in You too."
msgstr "pritisni Ti, pa Novac: tvoji računi, krediti i akcije. Banka koju vodiš je takođe u odeljku Ti."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.step3.to"
msgid "To find Banking"
msgstr "Da nađeš Bankarstvo"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.step4.how"
msgid "press Country, then Economy: public works and research."
msgstr "pritisni Država, pa Ekonomija: javni radovi i istraživanje."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.step4.to"
msgid "To find Development"
msgstr "Da nađeš Razvoj"

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.step5.how"
msgid "press You: what you hold and run, Settings and Help."
msgstr "pritisni Ti: ono što držiš i vodiš, Podešavanja i Pomoć."

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.step5.to"
msgid "To find the Menu"
msgstr "Da nađeš Meni"

#. Everyday words a player might type into Help's search to find this page, separated by commas. Give the words people in your language would search with, and add others if you like. Keep the commas.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.synonyms"
msgid "moved, where is, where did, today, work, press, banking, development, menu, dock, old, changed"
msgstr "premešteno, gde je, kuda, danas, rad, štampa, bankarstvo, razvoj, meni, traka, staro, promenjeno, promena"

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.title"
msgid "Where did things move?"
msgstr "Gde je šta premešteno?"

#. The meaning of the word before it, as a short sentence.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.word1.means"
msgid "One of the six: Home, Market, News, Country and You at the bottom of a phone, with Chat at its top; all six down the side of a desktop."
msgstr "Jedno od šest: Početna, Tržište, Vesti, Država i Ti na dnu telefona, a Ćaskanje na njegovom vrhu; svih šest sa strane na računaru."

#. A word this page explains, shown in bold above its meaning.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.moved.word1.term"
msgid "Place"
msgstr "Mesto"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.newspaper.line"
msgid "A paper's pieces, its writers and its printing money."
msgstr "Članci novina, njihovi novinari i novac za štampu."

#. {level} is a player level.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.newspaper.p1"
msgid "<b>Start one from You › Start something once you reach Level {level}.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Osnuj ih u odeljku Ti › Pokreni nešto kad dostigneš nivo {level}.</b>"

#. {creationFee} is the cost to start a paper, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.newspaper.p2"
msgid "To start it: give it a name and the country it prints from. It costs {creationFee}, which becomes its printing money. A citizen runs one paper at a time."
msgstr "Da ih osnuješ: daj im ime i državu iz koje se štampaju. To košta {creationFee}, što postaje novac za štampu. Građanin vodi samo jedne novine odjednom."

#. {printFee} is the cost to print one piece, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.newspaper.p3"
msgid "To publish: each piece costs the paper {printFee} to print. Add money under More options when it runs low."
msgstr "Da objaviš: štampanje svakog članka košta novine {printFee}. Dodaj novac u odeljku Još opcija kad ga ponestaje."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.newspaper.p4"
msgid "To take writers on: invite them from Writers, or accept those who ask. An editor publishes too; a writer sends you their pieces. What writers keep of a tip is yours to set, under More options."
msgstr "Da primiš novinare: pozovi ih iz odeljka Novinari ili prihvati one koji traže. Urednik takođe objavljuje; novinar ti šalje svoje članke. Koliko novinari zadržavaju od napojnice određuješ ti, u odeljku Još opcija."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.newspaper.title"
msgid "How do I run a newspaper?"
msgstr "Kako da vodim novine?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.offices.line"
msgid "Its offices, who holds them, and what each may do."
msgstr "Njene funkcije, ko ih drži i šta svaka sme."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.offices.p1"
msgid "<b>The players holding its offices: a head of state, a head of government, ministers and the members of the chamber.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Igrači koji drže njene funkcije: šef države, šef vlade, ministri i članovi Skupštine.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.offices.p2"
msgid "The constitution sets which offices exist and how each is filled: by election, by the chamber, or by an office that appoints to it."
msgstr "Ustav određuje koje funkcije postoje i kako se svaka popunjava: izborima, odlukom Skupštine ili preko funkcije koja na nju postavlja."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.offices.p3"
msgid "Each office’s page says how it is filled, how long a term lasts and what it may do, each power a door to where it is used."
msgstr "Stranica svake funkcije kaže kako se popunjava, koliko traje mandat i šta sme da radi, a svako ovlašćenje je vrata do mesta gde se koristi."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.offices.p4"
msgid "To see who holds what: Country, Politics, Offices. An office nobody holds says how it can be filled."
msgstr "Da vidiš ko šta drži: Država, Politika, Funkcije. Funkcija koju niko ne drži kaže kako može da se popuni."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.offices.p5"
msgid "If you hold one, its console is under You: what waits on it first, then what it may do."
msgstr "Ako držiš neku, njena konzola je pod Ti: prvo šta čeka nju, zatim šta sme da radi."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.offices.title"
msgid "Who runs a country?"
msgstr "Ko upravlja državom?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.orders.line"
msgid "What you have out on the Market, and what it holds."
msgstr "Šta imaš na Tržištu i šta to drži."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.orders.p1"
msgid "<b>An order or an offer waits until someone takes it, you take it back, or it ends, and while it waits it holds its money or goods.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Nalog ili ponuda čeka dok ga neko ne prihvati, dok ga ne povučeš ili dok ne istekne, a dok čeka, drži svoj novac ili robu.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.orders.p2"
msgid "To see them: open Your orders and offers in the Market. Open lists everything out in your name, what each one holds and when it ends."
msgstr "Da ih vidiš: otvori Tvoji nalozi i ponude na Tržištu. Otvoreno navodi sve što je postavljeno u tvoje ime, šta svaki drži i kada ističe."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.orders.p3"
msgid "To take one back: press Take back on an order, or Withdraw on an offer you sent. What it held comes back at once."
msgstr "Da povučeš jedan: pritisni Povuci na nalogu ili Povuci na poslatoj ponudi. Ono što je bilo zadržano vraća se odmah."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.orders.p4"
msgid "An order can fill while you are away, when a seller or a buyer meets your price. An offer to a person waits for their answer; if they say no, or do not answer in time, the goods come back."
msgstr "Nalog može da se ispuni dok te nema, kad prodavac ili kupac prihvati tvoju cenu. Ponuda osobi čeka njen odgovor; ako odbije ili ne odgovori na vreme, roba se vraća."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.orders.p5"
msgid "To see what you traded: open Records at the foot. Every closed order and answered offer is there, under its day."
msgstr "Da vidiš kakva je bila tvoja trgovina: otvori Zapise na dnu. Svaki zatvoren nalog i svaka ponuda na koju je odgovoreno nalaze se tamo, pod svojim danom."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.orders.p6"
msgid "Words: Set aside: money an offer to buy holds, still yours. Held: goods kept for an order or an offer until it ends."
msgstr "Pojmovi: Odvojeno: novac koji ponuda za kupovinu drži, i dalje tvoj. Zadržano: roba sačuvana za nalog ili ponudu dok se ne završi."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.orders.title"
msgid "What happens to my orders and offers?"
msgstr "Šta se dešava sa mojim nalozima i ponudama?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.organization.line"
msgid "A group with members and a voice."
msgstr "Grupa sa članovima i glasom."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.organization.p1"
msgid "<b>A group of players with a name, members and a voice: its leader and officers announce to every member. It has no power in the game.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Grupa igrača sa imenom, članovima i glasom: njen vođa i oficiri objavljuju svakom članu. Nema nikakvu moć u igri.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.organization.p2"
msgid "To join: open it from Country, People, Organizations. Some let anyone in; others decide each request."
msgstr "Da se pridružiš: otvori je iz odeljka Država, Ljudi, Organizacije. Neke primaju svakoga; druge odlučuju o svakom zahtevu."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.organization.p3"
msgid "To start one: You, Start something. It is free, and you lead it."
msgstr "Da osnuješ jednu: Ti, Pokreni nešto. Besplatno je, a ti je vodiš."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.organization.p4"
msgid "To leave: on its page, Leave. A leader cannot leave what they lead."
msgstr "Da napustiš: na njenoj stranici, Napusti. Vođa ne može da napusti ono što vodi."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.organization.p5"
msgid "Words: Officer: a member who can let people in, remove plain members and announce."
msgstr "Pojmovi: Oficir: član koji može da prima ljude, uklanja obične članove i objavljuje."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.organization.title"
msgid "What is an organization?"
msgstr "Šta je organizacija?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.party.line"
msgid "A label candidates share on the ballot."
msgstr "Oznaka koju kandidati dele na listiću."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.party.p1"
msgid "<b>A party is a label candidates share on the ballot. It gives no advantage and holds no power of its own.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Stranka je oznaka koju kandidati dele na listiću. Ne daje nikakvu prednost i ne drži sopstvenu moć.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.party.p2"
msgid "To ask to join: open it from Country, Politics, Parties and press Ask to join. You can ask several parties; you belong to the first that lets you in."
msgstr "Da zatražiš prijem: otvori je iz odeljka Država, Politika, Stranke i pritisni Zatraži prijem. Možeš da pitaš više stranaka; pripadaš prvoj koja te primi."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.party.p3"
msgid "To give money: on the party’s page, Money. Every gift is public and cannot be taken back, and the party fund cannot be spent yet."
msgstr "Da daš novac: na stranici stranke, Novac. Svaki dar je javan i ne može da se povuče, a fond stranke još ne može da se troši."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.party.p4"
msgid "To leave: on the party’s page, Leave. When its leader leaves, the party passes to its longest-serving officer."
msgstr "Da napustiš: na stranici stranke, Napusti. Kad vođa stranke ode, stranka prelazi na funkcionera sa najdužim stažom."

#. {level} is a player level. {fee} is the fee to found a party, drawn as a coin amount.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.party.p5"
msgid "To found one: from level {level}, for {fee}, under You, Start something."
msgstr "Da osnuješ stranku: od nivoa {level}, za {fee}, pod Ti, Pokreni nešto."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.party.p6"
msgid "Words: Officer: a member who can let people in and remove plain members. Party fund: the money given to a party."
msgstr "Pojmovi: Oficir: član koji može da prima ljude i uklanja obične članove. Fond stranke: novac dat stranci."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.party.title"
msgid "What is a party for?"
msgstr "Čemu služi stranka?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.peace.line"
msgid "How a war ends."
msgstr "Kako se rat završava."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.peace.p1"
msgid "A war ends when one side accepts the other’s peace terms. Terms can hand provinces over and say who keeps what. Whoever holds that power in a country offers them; the other country accepts them, refuses them, or sends different terms back, which take their place."
msgstr "Rat se završava kad jedna strana prihvati mirovne uslove druge. Uslovi mogu da predaju oblasti i kažu ko šta zadržava. Ko god drži to ovlašćenje u nekoj državi, nudi ih; druga država ih prihvata, odbija ili šalje nazad drugačije uslove, koji zauzimaju njihovo mesto."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.peace.p2"
msgid "Terms stand until they are answered or withdrawn. After peace, either country may declare war again."
msgstr "Uslovi važe dok se na njih ne odgovori ili se ne povuku. Posle mira, svaka od država može ponovo da objavi rat."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.peace.title"
msgid "Peace terms"
msgstr "Uslovi mira"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.personPage.line"
msgid "A citizen's public record."
msgstr "Javni zapis građanina."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.personPage.p1"
msgid "<b>Their public record: who they are and what they have done.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Njihov javni zapis: ko su i šta je zabeleženo o njima.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.personPage.p2"
msgid "It shows their banner and picture, their name and title, their level and country, where they are, their own words, the seals they chose to show, their statistics and their record. Anyone can read it."
msgstr "Prikazuje njihov baner i sliku, ime i titulu, nivo i državu, gde se nalaze, njihove sopstvene reči, pečate odabrane za prikaz, statistiku i zapis. Svako može da ga čita."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.personPage.p3"
msgid "To change yours: open You, then Your page, and press Edit. Your picture, banner and words are set in Settings. On You, each fact others can also see says Public."
msgstr "Da promeniš svoju: otvori Ti, zatim Tvoja stranica, i pritisni Uredi. Tvoja slika, baner i reči postavljaju se u Podešavanjima. Na ekranu Ti, svaka činjenica koju mogu da vide i drugi nosi oznaku Javno."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.personPage.p4"
msgid "To choose the seals on show: in Achievements, turn on Show on my page. You get room for more as you level up."
msgstr "Da izabereš pečate koji se prikazuju: u Dostignućima uključi Prikaži na mojoj stranici. Sa svakim novim nivoom dobijaš mesta za još."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.personPage.title"
msgid "What does a citizen's page show?"
msgstr "Šta prikazuje stranica građanina?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.press.line"
msgid "Newspapers written by players."
msgstr "Novine koje pišu igrači."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.press.p1"
msgid "<b>News is the papers players write, as headlines you open and read.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Vesti su novine koje pišu igrači, kao naslovi koje otvaraš i čitaš.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.press.p2"
msgid "To read: open a headline. A dot marks one you have not opened yet. Your country shows your country’s papers (press its flag to read another country’s), The world shows every paper, and Following shows the papers you follow."
msgstr "Da čitaš: otvori naslov. Tačka označava naslov koji još nije otvoren. Tvoja država prikazuje novine tvoje države (pritisni njenu zastavu da čitaš novine druge države), Svet prikazuje sve novine, a Praćenje novine koje pratiš."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.press.p3"
msgid "To keep up with a paper: press Follow on its front page or under one of its pieces. Its new pieces then come to Following. Pieces you liked are kept there too."
msgstr "Da pratiš novine: pritisni Prati na njihovoj naslovnoj strani ili ispod nekog njihovog članka. Njihovi novi članci tada stižu u Praćenje. Tamo se čuvaju i članci koji ti se sviđaju."

#. {level} is a player level.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.press.p4"
msgid "To write: if you write for a paper, Write is under the tabs. Anyone can start a paper from Level {level}."
msgstr "Da pišeš: ako pišeš za neke novine, Piši je ispod kartica. Svako može da osnuje novine od nivoa {level}."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.press.title"
msgid "How does News work?"
msgstr "Kako rade Vesti?"

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.primeMinister.line"
msgid "The head of government, and the powers of the office."
msgstr "Šef vlade i ovlašćenja funkcije."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.primeMinister.p1"
msgid "<b>A Prime Minister heads the government. What the office may do is set by the country’s constitution and listed on its page.</b>"
msgstr "<b>Premijer je na čelu vlade. Šta funkcija sme da radi određuje ustav države i navedeno je na njenoj stranici.</b>"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.primeMinister.p2"
msgid "Its powers often include appointing ministers, proposing bills and spending from the Treasury up to a limit the law sets. A power the office lacks is shown with who holds it instead."
msgstr "Njena ovlašćenja često uključuju postavljanje ministara, predlaganje zakona i trošenje iz državne kase do granice koju postavlja zakon. Ovlašćenje koje funkciji nedostaje prikazuje se uz onoga ko ga drži."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.primeMinister.p3"
msgid "To act: open the office’s console under You. What waits on it comes first, then its powers in groups, each act asking before it is done."
msgstr "Da deluješ: otvori konzolu funkcije pod Ti. Prvo je ono što čeka nju, zatim njena ovlašćenja po grupama, a svaka radnja pita pre nego što se izvrši."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.primeMinister.p4"
msgid "Words: Head of government: the office that runs the country day to day."
msgstr "Pojmovi: Šef vlade: funkcija koja svakodnevno vodi državu."

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.primeMinister.title"
msgid "What does a Prime Minister do?"
msgstr "Šta radi premijer?"

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.rankings.after"
msgid "Wealth shows your position only. No amount of anybody's money is ever shown."
msgstr "Bogatstvo prikazuje samo tvoj položaj. Iznos ničijeg novca se nikad ne prikazuje."

#, fuzzy,machine-translated
msgctxt "help.rankings.answer"
